    },
    "message": "fix(installer): don't verify the full command list when a deferred finish is pending\n\nWhen a coding agent is running, Windows uv aborts partway through the shim\nwrites (os error 32 on the running launcher's own shim), so the not-yet-finished\ncommands (mcc-rtk, mcc-desktop, ...) are never created. The installer staged the\nrest but then still ran the full command-family verification loop, which threw\n\"did not create mcc-rtk\" and crashed the install.\n\nConfigure-AndConfirmFreeClaudeCode now skips the full shim list when\nNeedDeferredFinish is set: it verifies only mcc-server if it landed, otherwise\nreports \"staged\" and returns. The non-deferred path is unchanged.\n\nTest: test_install_ps1_configure_confirm_tolerates_deferred_finish (proved to\nfail against the pre-fix script, pass with the fix).\n\nVerification: full suite 4108 passed / 6 pre-existing PS-installer failures\n(baseline unchanged).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
